    <!-- 09 Building an AI-Augmented Workflow -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="workflow">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">09 &mdash; Building an AI-Augmented Workflow</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">How to combine AI tools with human creators</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Start with scripting AI, then add editing AI, then explore generation tools</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">The goal is more output per creator-hour, not fewer creators</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Build quality control checkpoints between AI steps and human steps</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The most effective content operations in 2026 do not choose between AI and humans. They build workflows where AI handles the repetitive, time-consuming parts and humans handle the creative, authentic parts. Here is the workflow we use at OKAD and recommend to brands building <a href="/canvas-ugc/" class="text-accent hover:underline">Canvas UGC programs</a>.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>Step 1 &mdash; AI-powered ideation:</strong> Use Claude or ChatGPT to generate 20-30 content concepts per week based on trending topics, competitor analysis, and brand messaging pillars. Feed in your top-performing content as examples. The AI generates hooks, angles, and rough outlines. A human content strategist reviews and selects the 10-15 best concepts.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>Step 2 &mdash; AI-assisted scripting:</strong> For each selected concept, the AI generates a full script draft including hook, body, and CTA. The creator reviews the script, adjusts the language to match their natural voice, and adds personal anecdotes or reactions that make the content feel genuine. This step takes 5-10 minutes per script instead of 30-60 minutes writing from scratch.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>Step 3 &mdash; Human filming:</strong> The creator films the video. This is the one step that remains fully human. Real face, real voice, real environment. Attempts to replace this step with AI avatars consistently underperform. The creator can batch-film 5-10 scripts in a single session.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>Step 4 &mdash; AI-powered post-production:</strong> Raw footage goes through CapCut or Descript for auto-captioning, silence removal, and pacing optimization. AI generates b-roll from Runway or Pika for transitions and visual interest. Color correction is automated. A human editor does a final quality check &mdash; typically 5-10 minutes per video instead of 30-60 minutes of manual editing.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>Step 5 &mdash; AI-driven repurposing:</strong> Top performers are fed back into Opus Clip for alternative cuts. ElevenLabs generates voiceovers in additional languages for international markets. The AI suggests posting times based on historical engagement data. One filming session produces 15-30 publishable assets across platforms and languages.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">This workflow consistently produces 3-5x more content per creator while keeping production costs under control. The key is that the human is never removed from the process &mdash; they are amplified by AI at every step. For a detailed look at the tools creators use across this workflow, see our <a href="/ugc-creator-tools/" class="text-accent hover:underline">UGC creator tools guide</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

