    <section class="guide-section" id="glossary">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">10 &mdash; Glossary</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Key terms</h2>
        <ul class="list-none p-0 space-y-2">
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[160px]">UGC</strong> User-generated content. Video, images, or text created by real users or creators rather than the brand itself.</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[160px]">AI Avatar</strong> A synthetic digital human generated by AI, capable of speaking scripted content with realistic lip sync and gestures.</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[160px]">Voice Cloning</strong> AI technology that replicates a specific person's voice from a short audio sample, enabling text-to-speech in that voice.</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[160px]">Text-to-Video</strong> AI models that generate video content from written text prompts (e.g., Runway, Sora, Pika).</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[160px]">Hook Rate</strong> The percentage of viewers who watch past the first 1-3 seconds. A critical performance metric for short-form UGC.</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[160px]">LLM</strong> Large language model. The AI architecture behind tools like ChatGPT and Claude, used for scriptwriting and content generation.</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[160px]">Auto-captioning</strong> AI-generated subtitles overlaid on video content. Increases accessibility and watch time on sound-off platforms.</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[160px]">Repurposing</strong> The process of converting one piece of content into multiple formats (e.g., long-form interview into short-form clips).</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[160px]">Canvas UGC</strong> A delivery model where creators post content on brand-owned social accounts. See <a href="/canvas-ugc/" class="text-accent hover:underline">Canvas UGC guide</a>.</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[160px]">Prompt Engineering</strong> The practice of crafting specific instructions for AI tools to produce desired outputs. Essential for scriptwriting and video generation.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

